# Web export (Godot must be available)

After **every completed user prompt** (any finished change that ships — gameplay, UI, docs that bump version, or process fixes that update the pack):

1. Confirm version is ahead of Claude’s latest Done entry and `origin/main` (see commit-and-push rule).
2. Run `bash tools/export-web.sh` (it installs Godot 4.3 + templates if missing, then exports).
3. Commit the updated `index.html`, `index.js`, `index.wasm` (if changed), `index.pck`, and the versioned `index-<ver>.pck` produced by the script.
4. Push the working branch **and** push that tip to `main` so GitHub Pages serves the new pack. The script cache-busts via `mainPack: index-<version>.pck` so browsers do not keep showing an old title-menu version.

Do **not** claim a version bump is live until the web export has been rebuilt and pushed to `main`.

If `godot` is missing mid-session, run `bash tools/ensure-godot.sh` first.
